    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a mix of fascination and frustration for me. I appreciate its logical structure and how it applies to real-world problems, especially in physics. However, my education level limited my depth of understanding, so I often feel like I'm scratching the surface. It's a subject I admire from afar but don't fully master.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, sometimes. Complex equations or advanced topics can overwhelm me, especially if I haven't practiced them in a while. But I also find that breaking problems into smaller steps helps ease my anxiety. It's more about confidence than innate ability for me.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I’ve used AI tools like online calculators and step-by-step solvers occasionally. They’re helpful for checking my work or understanding concepts faster, but I prefer hands-on practice over relying solely on technology. It’s a tool, not a replacement for learning.",
